From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 23:31:33 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 19/21] iommu/io-pgtable-arm: contiguous hint behind
 io_pgtable_arm.cont_hint

The previous commit (kernel-topics 54ec97300f6e, FROMLIST) advertises
the contiguous-hint group sizes in pgsize_bitmap and maps such groups
with the CONT bit set, for more IOTLB reach on GPU, camera and video
buffers (the system heap already hands out 2 MB / 64 KB chunks since
q91n).

Make it opt-in: io_pgtable_arm.cont_hint=0 (default, read-only) sets
IO_PGTABLE_QUIRK_ARM_NO_CONT_HINT on every LPAE table before its page
sizes are chosen, so pgsize_bitmap, the map and the unmap paths are the
ones of before (no CONT bit is ever written, so the new partial-unmap
check never triggers); 1 uses the hint.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/iommu/io-pgtable-arm.c | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/iommu/io-pgtable-arm.c b/drivers/iommu/io-pgtable-arm.c
index 01d98959c514f..4418703932eba 100644
--- a/drivers/iommu/io-pgtable-arm.c
+++ b/drivers/iommu/io-pgtable-arm.c
@@ -12,6 +12,7 @@
 #include <linux/atomic.h>
 #include <linux/bitops.h>
 #include <linux/io-pgtable.h>
+#include <linux/moduleparam.h>
 #include <linux/sizes.h>
 #include <linux/slab.h>
 #include <linux/types.h>
@@ -1042,12 +1043,24 @@ static void arm_lpae_restrict_pgsizes(struct io_pgtable_cfg *cfg)
 	cfg->pgsize_bitmap &= GENMASK_ULL(cfg->oas, 0);
 }
 
+/*
+ * The contiguous hint (CONT) groups are opt-in here: io_pgtable_arm.cont_hint=1
+ * advertises them in pgsize_bitmap and maps them tagged; 0 (default) treats every
+ * table as IO_PGTABLE_QUIRK_ARM_NO_CONT_HINT, i.e. maps as before.
+ */
+static bool cont_hint;
+module_param(cont_hint, bool, 0444);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(cont_hint, "Use the contiguous hint bit in LPAE IOMMU page tables (default off)");
+
 static struct arm_lpae_io_pgtable *
 arm_lpae_alloc_pgtable(struct io_pgtable_cfg *cfg)
 {
 	struct arm_lpae_io_pgtable *data;
 	int levels, va_bits, pg_shift;
 
+	if (!cont_hint)
+		cfg->quirks |= IO_PGTABLE_QUIRK_ARM_NO_CONT_HINT;
+
 	arm_lpae_restrict_pgsizes(cfg);
 
 	if (!(cfg->pgsize_bitmap & (SZ_4K | SZ_16K | SZ_64K)))
-- 
